Z||000008||theogre||08-10-2001||07:43 PM||||read in my cave.....<P>If you hooked up the vapor can wrong you have a vac problem. The lines are size code with the ports. make sure they are on the right TBI ports.<P>there is no fan switch on an 88 4 cyl. it's ECM controlled.<P>It might be any number of things. you said there's no vac leaks... did you check over the EGR and PCV valves. either one bad often means a vac leak.<P>All joints on the PCV line are to be clamped. don't over tighten or you'll damage the elbows.<P>Crank sensor is cheap. <P>Bad MAP does nasty things to these DIS motors. won't run worth a turd if that's dead.<P>buy/borrow an ECM scanner. (ECM tools article) These are esential tools for DIS motors.<P>try to find the ALLdata CD I mention in another thread. It's got the complete wiring for the DIS motor. It's the only source besides Helm's shop book. You'll need to register the CD for an 87 fiero to get the best coverage of the 88 motor in an 86 car.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 08-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||new fiero||08-11-2001||03:33 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by theogre:<BR><B>read in my cave.....<P>If you hooked up the vapor can wrong you have a vac problem. The lines are size code with the ports. make sure they are on the right TBI ports.<P>there is no fan switch on an 88 4 cyl. it's ECM controlled.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I made sure the right size hoses went to the right locations....  Drove the car after I rigged the fan to stay on...still had problems....  sounds like the MAP sensor can be a real problem if bad so I will replace that and then move on to coils......<P>could my cooling problem be because of a bad fan relay??  I think that that is the only thing left in the fan circuit???<P>Thanks you all for your inputs!!!!!<P>Andy<BR><P>------------------<BR>newfiero<BR>(swapping 88 L4 to 86 and having fun!)<BR>Yahoo! Messenger id: newfiero||||reg||1
Z||000010||starfighter007@msn.com||08-11-2001||03:42 PM||||yep  there should be a relay for that car.I thought there is a temp. switch also,but ogre says not on the 4 cyl. I am not real familiar with the 4 cyl.I hope that map sensor works out for you .let us know either way.<p>[This message has been edited by starfighter007@msn.com (edited 08-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||theogre||08-11-2001||08:40 PM||||Is it doing this when hot or constantly? Constantly, even from a cold start, eliminates some things. like over heating.<P>Just how did you connect the fan? did you put the old style fan switch into the block?<P>What do you mean you wired fan direct? <P>If you didn't tie it to the wire from ECM terminal Black 21 then it's not going work. Unless you rewired in the old style fan switch in which case it will run at 235F like always. (The ECM will turn it on at 225F)<P>To test the realy, ground the green wire that feeds the relay. (Can't count on the AC control since you altered the wiring.)<P>For giggles, pull the thermostat and see if it helps. (You are sure the system is full of coolant?)<P><BR>Is there a metal plate between the coils and top of the ignition module? If that plate is missing then the coils can over heat and crap out. My experience with that it took about 8-10 miles of driving for them to do that. (10-15 minutes of run time.)<P>If you can't find an ALLDATA CD then register an 87 Fiero with ALLDATA-DIY online service. It's $25, but its got all the wiring for that ECM. Haynes doesn't have any of it. I don't believe S(C)hilton does either.<P>I said 87 because it is the most compatible with the setup you have now.  <A HREF="http://www.alldata.com" TARGET=_blank>www.alldata.com</A>   The only other source of accurate data for that ECM is the 87 Helm service book. Other than headlights, nearly everything for 87 is the same as other years. ||||reg||1
Z||000012||new fiero||08-12-2001||10:49 AM||||More info,<P>First off the car started acting up when it got hot, 30 min drive to work.  Had to run it during the heat of day for about 40 min. which probably fried a coil.....<P>Started her up yesterday, didn't start right away but did eventually start...  tested the MAP sensor according to the AUTOZONE test booklet...  Map sensor appears to be OK.<P>I didn't modify any of the wiring harness, I just jumpered across the 2 pins that go to the transducer and the fan started.  Also, if it is hot enough the fan will kick on when I disconnect the cable from the transducer...  Does this make sense?!  if it is not connected then the circuit is open, RIGHT?!<P>According to the chiltons if jumpering the plug works then the sensor(transducer) is bad...which it is not!  I have had 3 different ones in there now.  Also the guage still doesn't read above 100 deg. no matter how long the car runs for......<P>I am thinking one of the coils are fried and I have a cooling problem.....What do you think?<P>Andy<P>------------------<BR>newfiero<BR>(swapping 88 L4 to 86 and having fun!)<BR>Yahoo! Messenger id: newfiero||||reg||1
Z||000013||new fiero||08-19-2001||10:07 AM||||All,  I found a hole/leak in my exhaust manifold before the O2 sensor...  Would that cause the car to backfire??<P>Andy<P>------------------<BR>newfiero<BR>(swapping 88 L4 to 86 and having fun!)<BR>Yahoo! Messenger id: newfiero||||reg||5
Z||000014||theogre||08-19-2001||12:09 PM||||busted manifold will cause several problems. it screws up the output from the O2 sensor.<P>So what you are saying it that you rigged the old fan swtich into the new motor? In that case the switch doesn't actvate until 235F.<P>It still sounds like the fan wire is screwed up. The DIS ECM controls the fan in the DIS motor cars. As neer as I can tell, It's got a wire that runs to C500 to do it. (There is more than one terminal available in C500 for the fan control.) The ECM wil activate the fan at 225F.<P>Without seeing just what you've done, I can't guess any more than that. <P>The over heating problem can be any of a bunch of things. The fan is actually the least of that problem. You've got a plumbing problem or maybe a bad thermostat or water pump.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 08-19-2001).]||||reg||1
